//RS /// D-DET1: methods on the deterministic injected `Clock` capability.
//RS /// `clock.now()` reads the clock's current value (ms); `clock.tick(ms)` advances
//RS /// it by a relative span and returns the new value. Reproducible — the clock
//RS /// starts from the seed the caller supplied to `Clock.new(seed)` and only moves
//RS /// via explicit advances.
//RS ///
//RS /// D-DET-CAPAPI widens the surface: `clock.advance(to_ms)` sets the clock to an
//RS /// ABSOLUTE instant (returns the new value); `clock.wait(d: Duration)` advances
//RS /// by a `Duration` (relative, returns the new value).
